## Diagnosis

Path A reduced per-chunk macro expansion cost (each chunk is tiny -- 4-9 lines of trivial arithmetic), but the **wrapper itself is still one large `#[cube] fn` with 3221 sequential statements**. The wrapper's macro expansion holds:
- 3221 `syn::Stmt::Local` nodes
- 3221 `ExprCall` RHS expressions (each with ~15-40 path args)
- 3221 Scope entries (variable name registration)
- Plus intermediate `quote!` token streams during expansion

This still accumulates multi-GB working set. Approximate peak: 15-18 GB observed, but kernel OOM-killer fires only when allocation requests EXCEED available memory -- so true peak is higher, just unobservable.

## Next-step options surfaced

A. **(current) Lift wrapper cap** -> done, insufficient.
B. **Hierarchical / recursive sub-wrappers** -- group N chunks into a sub-wrapper, top wrapper calls sub-wrappers. Reduces top-level statement count ~12x. Cross-sub-wrapper live-set may still exceed 12-tuple ABI in dense 4th-derivative -- requires smart cross-boundary analysis.
C. **Wide-struct ABI** -- `#[derive(CubeType)] struct` with hundreds of fields. Untested in CubeCL 0.10 (existing comment in cse.py:34 verifies tuples <=12 fail, says nothing about structs).
D. **Local `Array<F>` scratch** -- chunks read/write a shared local array. ABI untested.
E. **Defer tpssloc from default-members** -- exclude from build by default. Plan 11.1-03 G3 canary (`mgga_c_b94`) doesn't need tpssloc. G4 oracle would need workaround.

